  "subject": "claims",
  "description": "One claim per group of lines, a service line for each, under the submitter, receiver and billing provider loops the 837P requires and with the payer on every subscriber. A claim for a dependent names the subscriber, then the patient in a loop of their own (HL 23, PAT, NM1*QC); a subscriber's own claim has no patient loop. Every position that carries data names a rule; positions holding X12's own vocabulary carry a const. CLM02 is the claim's lines added up, and HL and LX number themselves. Submitter, receiver, billing provider and payer are constants to set for a real trading relationship. Consecutive claims of one subscriber share their subscriber loop (2000B), and of one patient their patient loop (2000C): a segment's \"loop\" names the loop it is in, and the loop's first segment says by \"once_per\" which elements make it the same one.",
